            <ArticleTitle>Dorsal root entry zone coagulation for intractable sciatica.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>206-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic back and leg pain which is unresponsive to medical and/or surgical treatment is a common and difficult neurosurgical problem. Twelve patients with this condition underwent dorsal root entry zone coagulation of that region of the conus medullaris which correlated with the pain. Only 2 patients had a favorable result. The implications of this finding are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
